warning[LINT012]: `In(b)` passes `b` unquoted, not the state ID `'b'`
 --> tests/ui/lint012-in-unquoted-state-id.scx:8:37
  |
8 |     <transition event="go" cond="In(b)" target="b"/>
  |                                  ----- in this `cond` on `<transition>`
  |                                     ^ not a string
  |
  = note: in ECMAScript, `b` is a variable reference, not the state ID (no `<data id="b">` declares it, so evaluating it raises `error.execution` unless a script defines it); `In()` takes the state ID as a string
  = help: quote the state ID: `In('b')`
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions
